	Today I had a fairly high level (13) wizard going with a fair
	amount of cool stuff, etc. doing quite well before I stepped on
	that land mine on level 26 and along came Medusa ...

	(possible spoiler ...)



	Anyway, the strangest thing that happened in this game was having
	Excalibur taken away (?) by my god.  I had gotten a long sword a
	while back, and dipped it, giving me "a long sword named Excalibur".
	I had a luckstone, and through lots of sacrifice, soon picked up
	Dragonbane and Frost Brand as well.  Ex was enchanted the highest,
	so I was wielding it most of the time.  Since my luck was good, and
	I hadn't prayed in a while, I decided I might get some stuff blessed
	(notably my 3 potions of gain ability), so I prayed:

		a voice booms out, "I crown thee the Hand of Elbereth!"

	or some such sillyness, and I thought, "cool."  However, imagine my
	surprise when my next inventory revealed:

		X - a blessed +1 longsword

	I wasn't quite sure, but it seemed to be less effective thereafter.
	What gives?

